# Cursor done → Home Assistant push

When the user **explicitly** asks to be notified (e.g. “notify me”, “ping me”, “push when finished”), send **one** companion push after this turn’s work finishes (success or failure). Never notify by default. Skip for clarifications-only or plan discussion with no execution.

## Recipient

Zlatko’s phone only — do not fan out.

## Character limits (hard)

Match house companion limits:

- **Title ≤ 50 characters**
- **Message ≤ 100 characters**

Truncate with `…` if needed. Put detail in the chat reply, not the push.

## Media

1. **Always** set Cursor branding: `icon_url: /local/cursor-notify-icon.png`.
2. **Optionally** attach a visual when it clarifies the outcome (UI result, error dialog, before/after):
   - Prefer a **PNG screenshot**; use a short **GIF** only when motion helps more than a still.
   - Write the file under `homeassistant/www/cursor-notify/` (e.g. `done-<yyyyMMdd-HHmmss>.png` or `.gif`).
   - Sync to live HA **before** calling notify (see below) so the phone can load `/local/cursor-notify/<file>`.
   - Set `data.image` to that `/local/...` path. Omit `image` when there is no useful visual — do not invent decorative media.
3. On Android, `image` is the large attachment (may replace the small icon); still send `icon_url`. Keep attachments small (well under ~10 MB).

## Sync (required when icon/media paths must resolve)

From the My-Futuristic-Home repo root after adding/updating files under `homeassistant/www/`:

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/sync_homeassistant_config.ps1
```

## Notify call (Home Assistant MCP)

```text
ha_call_service:
  domain: notify
  service: mobile_app_zlatko_galaxy
  service_data:
    title: "<≤50 chars, usually Cursor or Cursor: <gist>>"
    message: "<≤100 chars outcome + task gist>"
    data:
      icon_url: /local/cursor-notify-icon.png
      channel: Cursor
      # image: /local/cursor-notify/<file.png|gif>   # only when attached
```

If `mobile_app_zlatko_galaxy` returns HTTP 400, retry once with the live service name that targets Zlatko’s companion (entity `notify.zlatko_galaxy`); keep the same `data` shape — do not drop the icon/image.

## Failure

If the MCP notify call fails, mention it once in the chat reply. No retry loops.
